 "story": "The map shows one risk: SPF at cognifit.com includes ses.amazonaws.com, which publishes no SPF record. Google Workspace receives the domain's mail and has a DKIM key in place to sign it. Four other services are set up to send as the domain: two transactional (Amazon SES, SendGrid), one marketing (Mailchimp), one support and CRM (Salesforce); one more is likely from a DKIM key name alone (Resend). One service shows an account and nothing set up to send (Microsoft 365). Not checked: the website (turned off) and the crt.sh certificate log (read only with --ct)."
